Organising a seminar at a château means offering your teams something other than a windowless hotel room. In the countryside, away from distractions, in a place you take over entirely: the setting changes the way people work together. At the Château de la Huberdière, in Touraine near Amboise, your company has a fourteen-hectare estate reserved for it alone, 2 hrs 20 from Paris.

This guide brings together what you need to know before booking a residential corporate seminar: capacities, workspaces, accommodation, catering and team-building activities.

## Why choose a seminar at a château

A successful seminar comes down to two things: the quality of the work produced and the team spirit that comes out of it. A château in the countryside works on both. The change of scene lifts teams out of the office routine. Private hire creates a sense of being among yourselves that encourages open speech. And the nature all around slows the pace just enough for ideas to flow.

La Huberdière is not a standardised seminar centre. It is a lived-in sixteenth-century family home, where your teams are welcomed as guests. That difference is felt: we do not run one group after another, we host yours.

## Flexible workspaces

The estate offers several meeting configurations, depending on the size of the group and the format of the day.

- The Orangery, 200 sq m bathed in light, for plenaries and large-group workshops
- Four more intimate lounges for breakout groups, interviews or quiet moments
- The grounds and the terrace for open-air sessions, when the weather allows

The technical logistics follow: wifi, sound system and screens are available. You arrive with your programme, we set up the rooms to your needs, in a U-shape, in islands or in a circle.

## Housing and feeding your teams on site

The residential seminar has one decisive advantage: no one leaves in the evening. Conversations carry on over dinner, team spirit is built outside the meetings. The château houses up to 20 people in 10 rooms, each with a private bathroom.

At the table, the cooking is homemade. Lodovica, Italian by birth, puts together meals from market and kitchen-garden produce, and caters to everyone's dietary needs. The packages range from a study day to a full stay of several days, from 70 € excl. VAT per person. We draw up a precise quote based on the length, the number of participants and the activities chosen.

## Team building at the château and in Touraine

Team spirit cannot be decreed in a meeting room. Around the château, there is no shortage of chances to bring a team together, and we book the activities with our local partners.

- An Italian cookery class with Lodovica, to prepare and share together
- A hot-air balloon flight at sunrise, taking off from the estate
- A canoe trip down the Cher, or a bike ride on the Loire à Vélo route
- A tasting in the cellars of Vouvray and Montlouis-sur-Loire
- A château visit, from Amboise and Clos Lucé to Chenonceau

These informal moments are often worth as much as the working sessions. They create shared memories and change how colleagues see one another.

## A corporate seminar 2 hrs 20 from Paris

The château's location makes it an easy-to-reach base for a seminar in Touraine. Allow about 2 hrs 20 by road from Paris, or one hour by TGV to Saint-Pierre-des-Corps then thirty minutes by car. Far enough for a change of scene, close enough to come without losing a day.

To discover the packages, the spaces and the capacities in detail, head to the [seminar at the château](/en/seminaire) page. And if you extend the stay, our guide to [visiting the Loire Valley châteaux](/en/blog/visiter-chateaux-de-la-loire) will help your teams make the most of the region.

Tell us your dates, the size of the group and the spirit of the seminar: we will send you a tailored proposal within 24 hours.
